---
The 11-stage request pipeline

Every request to /v1/chat traverses these in order. Each stage i / redact / re-route / deny, and each records its own latency_msinto a HopRecord:

1. JWT Auth (middleware/auth.py) — HS256 bearer token, extracts user_id + role (admin/analyst/guest). No anonymous path.
2. Rate Limit (middleware/rate_limit.py) — in-memory sliding win/ analyst 20 / guest 5 per minute. Framed as "the firstcost-control stage."
3. Sanitize (scanning/sanitize.py) — NFKC normalization + homoglth → ASCII) + zero-width character stripping. Defeats exact-matchscanner evasion (e.g. a Cyrillic "і" in "іgnore").
4. PII Scan (scanning/pii.py) — two-layer (detailed below), circlosed.
5. Injection Scan (scanning/injection.py) — ~51 regex patterns + token-splitting + leetspeak normalization.                                          6. Risk Score (scanning/risk.py) — capped aggregation of all fincore.
7. Classifier (backends/classifier.py) — assigns complexity_tier + intent_class. This is "Hop 1" of the compound pipeline.                           8. OPA Policy (policy/opa_client.py) — sends full context to OPAroute. Fail-closed.
9. Model Routing (policy/router.py) — resolves the final model string from role + risk + OPA + complexity.                                           10. FM Backend (backends/ollama.py) — the actual generation callal token counts + latency.
11. Output Scan (scanning/output.py) — 16 secret/credential patterns + Shannon-entropy check on the model's response before returning it.            
The pipeline is fail-closed by design: a dependency failure (Presidio down, OPA unreachable) results in denial, never silent pass-through — with one deliberate, documented exception (see routing below).

